{
	"_about": "The lands round the farm and Maple Grove (scripts/regions.gd builds them). walk: where Nora may go, [x, z, width, depth] in metres. grass: how its grass blades differ from the farm's (scripts/grass.gd set_lands): density and height as shares of the farm's, seed_heads the share of stems gone to seed, tint a colour to multiply the farm's blades by (else the land's colours against the farm's grass), tint_share how much of that tint they take; the beach's 0 leaves only the fringe where its sand meets the grass. ground: the patch of ground drawn under it (wider than walk, so its edge fades out of sight into the grass), with three colours mixed by noise. scatter: [model in assets/props or tree:<kind>, how many, scale min, scale max, gap between them in metres, blocker half-size in metres (0 = walk through)]. Each region's scenery is its own kind in the world editor (swamp-rock_cluster and so on), so it can be moved and saved like the rest. A scatter entry may end with a tint colour (multiplied into the model's colours: the dunes' sun-bleached rocks). seeded: each scatter entry draws from its own random numbers (seeded by the land and the model), so adding, removing or filling in a model never moves the rest; every land added from 2026-11-26 is seeded. extra: more scatter for a land made before then, placed after everything else, seeded the same way, so the scenery already there stays where it was. relief (Alex, 2026-11-26: dunes and rolling hills): [x, z, half-width, half-length, height, turn in degrees] mounds raised in the land's ground; where one stands more than 12 cm high the walking grid is blocked (scripts/regions.gd mark_relief), so she walks the valleys and passes between them. The ground she walks on is still flat: true terrain she can climb is a later step. A dune (dunes: true) is steeper on its east, lee side. Until the swamp's own models exist (cattails, lily pads, snags, toadstools, ferns), stand-ins from the models there are (dark hedges, berry bushes, clover, short tufts; tinted) fill it; take them out when the real ones land. deep_mire (the swamp): an island ringed by deep black water (centre, size, moat width in metres) that blocks the walking grid until she owns mire waders from Steve (scripts/explore.gd).",
